# Only needed when the client and server are deployed on different origins (for example,
# client on Vercel, server on Railway, Render or Fly). Vercel cannot host the persistent
# WebSocket server. Leave unset for local development: the client falls back to same origin
# /ws, which the Vite proxy in vite.config.ts forwards to the local backend.
#
# Set this in the Vercel project's Environment Variables (Production), not in a committed file:
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://<your-server-host>/ws
